sons um and  remember that trump was conducting a  very kind of  racist anti-asian campaign  directed at the chinese at the time and  so it was difficult  to see this as anything more than a sort  of racist attack  when the who investigations team came  back  from china earlier this year the head of  the who said something quite interesting  he said all theories remained on the  table  and at the time the world's media had  been coming to the conclusion  uh that a natural origin was much more  likely  and he really kind of changed the tone  of the debate at that point and after  that  uh it seems to me scientists did feel  a lot more emboldened to say hang on a  minute  we do need to look into this a bit  further and we started to see  a decided shift in the scientific  community  if there has been a lab leak how will we  know if it was deliberate or accidental  well if the chinese were deliberately  going to  uh release a virus i think they would be  very foolish to do so  right next to um their institute of  virology  um you know presumably that they would  uh release this  uh this this virus next to the americans  institute for virology so i i just think  that um you know if you're going to  deliberately  bioengineer a weapon uh then then  releasing it just sort of right outside  the lab is a pretty dumb thing to do and  i don't think that they would have done  that  that's so good  is there any chance covert 19 was  man-made  and how can scientists tell this is  where  a lot of the hottest debate is actually  taking place  the virus has got oddities in its um  genetic makeup  at the same time you would expect it to  have auditors in its genetic makeup  because most viruses aren't suddenly  leaping out of bats and killing people  all around the world so  clearly it's going to be a virus of  concerning lethality  the question of whether that has come  about because of engineering  is one that people are really debating  at a molecular level  um in labs around the 